Rules:
  [E1] Use TLS 1.3 for data in transit.
  [E2] Use AES-256-GCM for data at rest.
  [E3] Use RSA-2048 or ECC for asymmetric encryption.
  [E4] Use HMAC for message integrity.
  [E5] Store keys in HSM or key management service.
  [E6] Rotate keys regularly.
  [E7] Never roll your own crypto.
  [E8] Use authenticated encryption (Encrypt-then-MAC).

Pros:
  - Data protection
  - Compliance
  - Trust

Cons:
  - Performance overhead
  - Key management
  - Complexity

Alternatives:
  - TLS (simpler)
  - Managed encryption (cloud)

State: +

